  "title": "Jurassic Bird Fossil Had Wings Too Short to Fly #shorts",
  "description": "Researchers led by Wang Min of the Chinese Academy of Sciences describe Yuezhuornis yangyuanensis in a study published in Nature on October 14, 2026. The bird lived roughly 150 million years ago in Fujian, China; its short forelimbs and ground-bird limb proportions point to a life on the ground, per the authors. It is known from a single incomplete specimen.\n\nSources: Nature paper (s41586-026-10972-z); South China Morning Post; Sci.News; CGTN; The Star.\n\n#science #paleontology #birds",
